Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the FreeTDS driver
============================================

qore-freetds-module contains the native DBI driver. The optional
qore-freetds-module-doc contains the shared Sybase/FreeTDS API reference and
example tests. Debhelper produces matching debug symbols. This build uses the
distribution freetds-dev CT-Library and explicitly disables the proprietary
Sybase OCS target; it does not install a server or modify FreeTDS configuration.

Build in an isolated native environment with the packaged Qore 3.0 runtime,
libqore-dev and Build-Depends from debian/control. The current qualification
target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64. Other Debian/Ubuntu releases, architectures,
Sybase OCS and Sybase ASE servers require separate qualification. Cross builds
are rejected because Qore executes during configuration and testing.

Source and build
----------------

The +ds orig tarball excludes only m4/acx_pthread.m4: this unused legacy
Autoconf macro contains no license grant. Keep the licensed C++ macros and
all source notices. CMake does not use Autoconf. From a clean checkout:

    version=1.4~git20260928.1+ds
    mkdir -p ../freetds-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-freetds-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' ':!m4/acx_pthread.m4' | xz > \
        "../freetds-package-work/qore-freetds-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../freetds-package-work/qore-freetds-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../freetds-package-work
    cp -a debian "../freetds-package-work/qore-freetds-module-$version/"
    cd "../freetds-package-work/qore-freetds-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory. With dependencies preinstalled, build
as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

-B produces architecture packages without Doxygen; -A produces documentation.
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc omits documentation; DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc omits the
HTML. Distribution compiler and hardening flags are preserved. Native Qore
modules resolve Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. Rules derive
the minimum runtime and libqore SONAME dependency from the installed SDK;
dh_shlibdeps supplies the FreeTDS and other library dependencies. Runtime is
not Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native Qore interpreter.

Tests and release qualification
-------------------------------

The default build and installed runtime tests run freetds-offline.qtest: driver
capabilities (including columnar results and BCP), invalid protocol and missing
username validation before network I/O, and unopened connection cleanup.
The installed compiler test builds and runs a fresh program away from the
source tree. This DBI driver uses Qore's Datasource compiler metadata and has
no user qmods or dependency trailers; ordinary dh_strip is appropriate.

The other test/*.qtest suites need a disposable live database. They create and
drop tables/procedures and must never run against production data. Set
QORE_DB_CONNSTR_FREETDS to a dedicated test database connection string, e.g.
'freetds:USER/PASSWORD@DATABASE%HOST:PORT', and explicitly preload the newly
built driver when running each suite. Some older tests have local developer
defaults: always supply this variable for qualification. No credentials are
shipped. Build tests do not download or start a proprietary SQL Server image;
perform live integration separately, retaining server/client versions and logs.
Microsoft SQL Server qualification does not qualify Sybase ASE or OCS.

Check source/binary Lintian, hardening and detached debug symbols, installation
without the SDK, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall,
and reproducibility from different paths and parallelism. Record exact source
commit and source/package hashes. Each changed upload needs a fresh version.
Testing PPA publication is separate from final general-release approval.
